= April 2025 — Who will defend the pilot?

[? if shorter_time_pilot_active: Employers and public institutions can apply
to a Labour-Ministry trial of shorter hours without cutting pay. Labour
Minister **[+ labor_minister +]** of **[+ labor_minister_party +]** can decide
whether unions help govern each workplace trial and whether independent
evaluators own the evidence.?]
[? if not shorter_time_pilot_active: Lewica does not control the Labour
Ministry, so no national trial starts automatically. Labour-policy organiser
<span class="party-lewica"><b>Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk</b></span>, trade unions and willing employers can draft a
pilot and collect voluntary evidence, but they cannot turn participation into
a government programme.?]

Workers need shorter hours without hidden work intensification. Employers want
subsidy and flexibility; the Finance Ministry wants productivity figures before
the promise expands. The pilot will either create institutions capable of
defending a later reform or become a slogan a later minister can bury.

- @time_union
- @time_union_opposition
- @time_evidence
- @time_headline

@time_union
title: Give unions a formal role in every workplace trial
subtitle: Make the pilot a school for bargaining; coalition liberals will call it union capture.
view-if: shorter_time_pilot_active = 1
on-arrival: labor_credibility += 5; union_trust += 6; opzz_cooperation += 4; labor_mobilization += 6; labor_dissent -= 4; workers_support += 4; razem_cooperation += 2; progressives_dissent -= 1; spring_dissent -= 1; barons_dissent += 1; ko_relation -= 2; psl_relation -= 1; government_coalition_dissent += 1; government_delivery += 2; news_headline = "The shorter-week pilot becomes a collective-bargaining school"

Every participating workplace must negotiate its trial with recognised worker
representatives and publish the agreement. Unions gain members and experience
rather than a consultation photograph; employers and coalition liberals warn
that the ministry has turned an experiment into organised labour policy.

- @poland_event_queue: File the union-governed pilot

@time_union_opposition
title: Have unions draft a pilot bill and audit comparable employers
subtitle: Non-ministerial route. Cost: 1 resource. Build evidence and a bill, not a national trial.
view-if: shorter_time_pilot_active = 0
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The caucus cannot staff the union audit.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; labor_credibility += 4; union_trust += 5; opzz_cooperation += 3; labor_mobilization += 5; labor_dissent -= 3; workers_support += 3; razem_cooperation += 1; progressives_dissent -= 1; media_capacity += 2; ko_relation -= 1; public_trust += 1; last_policy_stage = "Proposal"; last_policy_authority = "Lewica Pracy MPs and trade-union campaign"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Unions write a pilot bill and publish voluntary workplace evidence"

Union researchers recruit willing workplaces, audit hours and write the draft
national scheme. The evidence gives Lewica a bill and workers a campaign, not
a statutory trial. The cabinet can still decline to fund or recognise any of it.

- @poland_event_queue: File the opposition pilot proposal

@time_evidence
title: Use independent evaluation and publish productivity data
subtitle: Active ministry pilot: 1 budget capacity. Otherwise: 1 party resource for a voluntary evidence base.
